WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.412 --> 00:00:03.099
- We want to build a
company that releases toys

00:00:03.099 --> 00:00:05.620
that are educational and entertaining

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:10.132
and we want to do that one
really great toy at a time.

00:00:10.132 --> 00:00:13.252
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.252 --> 00:00:16.524
My name is Filippo Yacob,
I've always been a big kid,

00:00:16.524 --> 00:00:18.728
I've always liked toys,
I've always liked games.

00:00:18.728 --> 00:00:22.792
And when I found out that
I was gonna be a father,

00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:25.060
I thought it would be a good time

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.580
to start making toys for a living.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.380
And I wanted to make educational toys.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.220
I think toys have evolved
from simple objects

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:38.168
of entertainment into tools
for development for children.

00:00:38.168 --> 00:00:42.335
Our understanding of how
children develop and grow

00:00:43.191 --> 00:00:46.980
has changed the way that we
look at these tools as well

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.147
and I think we're at the
point where new kinds of toys

00:00:52.972 --> 00:00:56.212
that are truly educational
and entertaining

00:00:56.212 --> 00:00:57.984
can start being made
because of technologies

00:00:57.984 --> 00:01:01.431
and I just wanted to be
at the forefront of that.

00:01:01.431 --> 00:01:03.202
My first toy is called
the Cubetto play set,

00:01:03.202 --> 00:01:05.438
it's the most crowdfunded
educational technology

00:01:05.438 --> 00:01:07.342
invention in Kickstarter history.

00:01:07.342 --> 00:01:11.272
It has won a Red Dog
design award, best of best,

00:01:11.272 --> 00:01:14.064
a Cannes Lion Gold for product design,

00:01:14.064 --> 00:01:17.814
it's toured the MoMA in
New York City and MIT

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:21.938
and it's a tangible programming
interface for children.

00:01:21.938 --> 00:01:26.288
It's a wooden robot that
merges Logo Turtle-inspired

00:01:26.288 --> 00:01:29.666
programming with Montessori-based
hands-on learning,

00:01:29.666 --> 00:01:31.792
so it's a wooden robot
that children can program

00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:35.004
using blocks instead of a screen or text.

00:01:35.004 --> 00:01:37.837
I think I'm fairly self-motivated,

00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:41.256
I really really wanna make
great products and great toys.

00:01:41.256 --> 00:01:43.822
But I think what kind of
gave me the inspiration

00:01:43.822 --> 00:01:46.946
and changed my attitude
towards work and design

00:01:46.946 --> 00:01:50.812
and life in general was
having my own children.

00:01:50.812 --> 00:01:53.212
I have a three-year-old
son who was actually born

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:55.717
on the day that this company was launched.

00:01:55.717 --> 00:01:58.120
We would like to see a Cubetto play set

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.856
in each of the 2.4 million
or so early-learning centers

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:06.365
and libraries and primary
schools around the world.

00:02:06.365 --> 00:02:08.858
And then new products, we have
new products in the pipeline,

00:02:08.858 --> 00:02:13.612
new services, and expanding
the range of products

00:02:13.612 --> 00:02:16.000
and services that we can
offer to our community

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.751
with the same dedication
that we had building this one

00:02:20.751 --> 00:02:23.334
and sticking to our principles.

